-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 41: DEBENTURE HOLDERS' ACTION: RECEIVER'S REGISTER (part roc9, layer 1).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  Every decision function answers MAYBE BOOLEAN.
--   JUST TRUE    the text says yes on these facts.
--   JUST FALSE   the text says no in its own words (a flat negative, "only", an "if" or "where" that is
--                unmet, a period the text fixes in its own words, a definition that says "means").
--   NOTHING      the text does not answer: it is silent, or a power or a scope is limited by its own
--                wording, or a bare "must" is plainly not met (the text says what is required, and not
--                what follows).  A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Each branch carries a FALSE-kind or NOTHING-kind comment saying which.
--
-- "FORK" lines mark the sites of the six open convention questions (QA to QE) and the marginal readings;
-- work/forks.py collects them into NOTES.md.
-- Order 41 has one period (rule 2(3)): it is stated as a Period of the core and compared with the last day
-- that Order 3, Rule 3 (part roc1) computes, which is taken as an input.

§ `Order 41 -- Debenture holders' action: receiver's register`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 41 Rule 1 -- the receiver's register`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Who acts under this Order, and what they do.  One party type and one action type serve every regulative
-- rule of the Order; each constructor is labelled with the rule that needs it.
DECLARE `o 41 r 1 party` IS ONE OF
    `o 41 r 1 the receiver`
    `o 41 r 6(2) the solicitor of the claimant or the person the Court directs`

DECLARE `o 41 r 1 action` IS ONE OF
    `o 41 r 1 keep the receiver's register`
    `o 41 r 6(2)(a) endorse a memorandum of payment on the debenture or debenture stock certificate`
    `o 41 r 6(2)(b) make and sign the certificate and send it to the Accountant-General`

-- "Every receiver appointed by the Court in an action to enforce registered debentures or registered
-- debenture stock must, if so directed by the Court, keep a register".  Scope: a receiver of that kind
-- (a scope limit with no "only": outside it the answer is NOTHING).  Condition: "if so directed".
-- src:5814 | 1. Every receiver appointed by the Court in an action to enforce registered debentures or registered debenture stock must, if so directed by the Court, keep a register of transfers of, and other transmissions of title to, such debentures or stock (called in this Order the receiver’s register).
@ref O 41 r 1 (src:5814)
GIVEN `the receiver was appointed by the Court in an action to enforce registered debentures or registered debenture stock` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has directed the receiver to keep a register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 41 r 1 the duty to keep a receiver's register arises` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `the receiver was appointed by the Court in an action to enforce registered debentures or registered debenture stock`)
           THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every receiver appointed by the Court in an action to enforce registered debentures or registered debenture stock"
           IF (NOT `the Court has directed the receiver to keep a register`)
           THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, if so directed by the Court, keep a register"
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The duty itself, as a regulative rule.  The text gives it no time limit and no consequence.
-- src:5814 | 1. Every receiver appointed by the Court in an action to enforce registered debentures or registered debenture stock must, if so directed by the Court, keep a register of transfers of, and other transmissions of title to, such debentures or stock (called in this Order the receiver’s register).
@ref O 41 r 1 (src:5814)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `o 41 r 1 party` `o 41 r 1 action`
`o 41 r 1 the receiver's duty to keep the register` MEANS
    PARTY `o 41 r 1 the receiver`
    MUST `o 41 r 1 keep the receiver's register`

-- "(called in this Order the receiver's register)".  A label for the register the rule describes; it does
-- not say "means", so a register that does not fit the description is not answered.
-- FORK F41.1 | label "called": NOTHING for a register outside the description | JUST FALSE (read as "means")
-- src:5814 | 1. Every receiver appointed by the Court in an action to enforce registered debentures or registered debenture stock must, if so directed by the Court, keep a register of transfers of, and other transmissions of title to, such debentures or stock (called in this Order the receiver’s register).
@ref O 41 r 1 (src:5814)
GIVEN `it is a register of transfers of, and other transmissions of title to, such debentures or stock` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is kept by a receiver as Rule 1 requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 41 r 1 a register is the receiver's register` MEANS
    IF `it is a register of transfers of, and other transmissions of title to, such debentures or stock` AND `it is kept by a receiver as Rule 1 requires`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "(called in this Order the receiver's register)" names the register Rule 1 describes and does not say "means"

