§§ `Order 41 Rule 2 -- registration of transfers`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Rule 2(1): the receiver's duty to register arises "Where a receiver is required by Rule 1 to keep a
-- receiver's register, then, on the application of any person entitled ... by virtue of any transfer or
-- other transmission of title, and on production of such evidence of identity and title as the receiver
-- may reasonably require".  The "where", the application and the production are all conditions of the duty.
-- FORK F41.2 | "on the application ... and on production": treated as "where" (ruling (c) of 2026-11-05): JUST FALSE if unmet | NOTHING (a scope limit)
-- src:5816 | 2. —(1) Where a receiver is required by Rule 1 to keep a receiver’s register, then, on the application of any person entitled to any debentures or debenture stock by virtue of any transfer or other transmission of title, and on production of such evidence of identity and title as the receiver may reasonably require, the receiver must, subject to paragraphs (2) and (3), register the transfer or other transmission of title in that register. (2) Before registering a transfer, the receiver must, unless the due execution of the transfer is proved by affidavit, send by post to the registered holder of the debentures or debenture stock transferred at the holder’s registered address a notice stating — ( a )
@ref O 41 r 2(1) (src:5816)
GIVEN `the receiver was appointed by the Court in an action to enforce registered debentures or registered debenture stock` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has directed the receiver to keep a register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a person entitled to debentures or debenture stock by virtue of a transfer or other transmission of title has applied for registration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that person has produced such evidence of identity and title as the receiver may reasonably require` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 41 r 2(1) the receiver's duty to register the transfer or other transmission of title arises` MEANS
    CONSIDER `o 41 r 1 the duty to keep a receiver's register arises` `the receiver was appointed by the Court in an action to enforce registered debentures or registered debenture stock` `the Court has directed the receiver to keep a register`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        BRANCH IF (NOT `a person entitled to debentures or debenture stock by virtue of a transfer or other transmission of title has applied for registration`)
               THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on the application of any person entitled to any debentures or debenture stock by virtue of any transfer or other transmission of title"
               IF (NOT `that person has produced such evidence of identity and title as the receiver may reasonably require`)
               THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on production of such evidence of identity and title as the receiver may reasonably require"
               OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a receiver is required by Rule 1 to keep a receiver's register"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the receiver is outside Rule 1's scope, so Rule 1 has not answered

-- Rule 2(2), first limb: before registering a transfer, the receiver must send the notice, "unless the due
-- execution of the transfer is proved by affidavit".  The exception lifts the duty: it does not arise.
-- "a transfer" is the scope: other transmissions of title are not mentioned in paragraph (2).
