-- Rule 2(2), second limb: "no transfer may be registered until the period so specified has elapsed".
-- A bar with an "until" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (d)): JUST TRUE before the period has elapsed, JUST FALSE after.
-- The bar is tied to the notice, so it is asked only where a notice with a period was sent.
-- FORK F41.3 | the period "has elapsed" once its last day has passed (registration on the last day is still barred) | elapsed at the start of the last day
-- src:5819 | that the transfer will be registered unless within the period specified in the notice the holder informs the receiver that the holder objects to the registration, and no transfer may be registered until the period so specified has elapsed.
@ref O 41 r 2(2) (src:5819)
GIVEN `a notice specifying a period was sent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which registration is proposed` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period specified in the notice` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 41 r 2(2) the transfer cannot yet be registered` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `a notice specifying a period was sent`)
           THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the bar speaks of "the period so specified" in the notice; no notice was sent
           IF `the date on which registration is proposed` AT MOST `the last day of the period specified in the notice`
           THEN JUST TRUE -- the bar still holds: "until the period so specified has elapsed"
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no transfer may be registered until the period so specified has elapsed" (the period has elapsed, so the bar is over)

-- Rule 2(3): "The period to be specified in the notice ... must be at least 14 days after a reply from the
-- registered holder would in the ordinary course of post reach the receiver if the holder had replied to
-- the notice on the day following the day when in the ordinary course of post the notice would have been
-- delivered at the place to which it was addressed."
-- src:5820 | (3) The period to be specified in the notice mentioned in paragraph (2) must be at least 14 days after a reply from the registered holder would in the ordinary course of post reach the receiver if the holder had replied to the notice on the day following the day when in the ordinary course of post the notice would have been delivered at the place to which it was addressed.
@ref O 41 r 2(3) (src:5820)
`o 41 r 2(3) the minimum period after a reply would reach the receiver` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- FORK F41.4 | "if the holder had replied to the notice on the day following the day when ... the notice would have been delivered": the reply goes on the day after delivery and then takes the days of post, so it reaches the receiver on the delivery day plus 1 plus the days of post | the days of post counted from the delivery day itself (one day sooner)
-- The day a reply would reach the receiver: the notice is delivered on a day (in the ordinary course of
-- post), the holder replies on the day following, and the reply takes the usual days of post to arrive.
-- The days of post are a fact the asker states (the Rules do not fix them).
-- src:5820 | (3) The period to be specified in the notice mentioned in paragraph (2) must be at least 14 days after a reply from the registered holder would in the ordinary course of post reach the receiver if the holder had replied to the notice on the day following the day when in the ordinary course of post the notice would have been delivered at the place to which it was addressed.
@ref O 41 r 2(3) (src:5820)
GIVEN `the day the notice would in the ordinary course of post be delivered` IS A DATE
      `the days a reply would in the ordinary course of post take to reach the receiver` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`o 41 r 2(3) the day a reply would in the ordinary course of post reach the receiver` MEANS
    (`the day the notice would in the ordinary course of post be delivered` PLUS 1) PLUS `the days a reply would in the ordinary course of post take to reach the receiver`

-- Is the period specified in the notice long enough?  "at least 14 days after" is a period the text fixes in
-- its own words: a period that ends sooner is JUST FALSE.  The earliest permitted last day is counted by
-- Order 3, Rule 3 (part roc1) from the day a reply would reach the receiver: it is an input (S-T1b).
