-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 41 Rule 4 -- the receiver's register as evidence`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- "Any entry made in the receiver's register, if verified by an affidavit made by the receiver or by such other
-- person as the Court may direct, is in all proceedings in the action in which the receiver was appointed
-- evidence of the transfer or transmission of title to which the entry relates and, in particular, must be
-- accepted as evidence ... for the purpose of any distribution of assets, even though the transfer or
-- transmission has taken place after the making of a certificate in the action certifying the holders".
-- The "even though" limb adds no condition, so the day of the transfer is not asked.
-- MARGINAL a | "if verified": an entry that is not verified is JUST FALSE (a failed "if") | NOTHING (the text does not say an unverified entry is not evidence)
-- src:5826 | 4. Any entry made in the receiver’s register, if verified by an affidavit made by the receiver or by such other person as the Court may direct, is in all proceedings in the action in which the receiver was appointed evidence of the transfer or transmission of title to which the entry relates and, in particular, must be accepted as evidence of the transfer or transmission for the purpose of any distribution of assets, even though the transfer or transmission has taken place after the making of a certificate in the action certifying the holders of the debentures or debenture stock certificates.
@ref O 41 r 4 (src:5826)
GIVEN `the entry is made in the receiver's register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are proceedings in the action in which the receiver was appointed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entry is verified by an affidavit made by the receiver` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entry is verified by an affidavit made by another person the Court has directed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 41 r 4 the entry is evidence of the transfer or transmission of title` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `the entry is made in the receiver's register`) OR (NOT `the proceedings are proceedings in the action in which the receiver was appointed`)
           THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any entry made in the receiver's register ... in all proceedings in the action in which the receiver was appointed"
           IF `the entry is verified by an affidavit made by the receiver` OR `the entry is verified by an affidavit made by another person the Court has directed`
           THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if verified by an affidavit made by the receiver or by such other person as the Court may direct"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 41 Rule 5 -- proof of title of the holder of a bearer debenture`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Rule 5(1): "This Rule applies in relation to an action to enforce bearer debentures or to enforce debenture
-- stock in respect of which the company has issued debenture stock bearer certificates."  A scope limit.
-- src:5828 | 5. —(1) This Rule applies in relation to an action to enforce bearer debentures or to enforce debenture stock in respect of which the company has issued debenture stock bearer certificates. (2) Even though judgment has been given in the action and a certificate has been made in the action certifying the holders of such debentures or certificates referred to in paragraph (1), the title of any person claiming to be such a holder is (in the absence of notice of any defect in the title) sufficiently proved by the production of the debentures or debenture stock certificates (as the case may be) together with a certificate of identification signed by the person producing the debenture or certificate — ( a )
@ref O 41 r 5(1) (src:5828)
GIVEN `the action is to enforce bearer debentures` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action is to enforce debenture stock in respect of which the company has issued debenture stock bearer certificates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 41 r 5(1) this Rule applies to the action` MEANS
    IF `the action is to enforce bearer debentures` OR `the action is to enforce debenture stock in respect of which the company has issued debenture stock bearer certificates`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an action to enforce bearer debentures or to enforce debenture stock in respect of which the company has issued debenture stock bearer certificates"

-- Rule 5(2): the title of a person claiming to be a holder "is (in the absence of notice of any defect in the
-- title) sufficiently proved by the production of the debentures or debenture stock certificates ... together
-- with a certificate of identification signed by the person producing the debenture or certificate" that
-- identifies it and certifies the name and address of the holder.  "Even though judgment has been given" adds
-- no condition.  Sufficiency is not exclusivity: another way of proving title is not excluded.
-- MARGINAL a | "(in the absence of notice of any defect in the title)": a condition on the statement that title is sufficiently proved, so with notice of a defect the statement fails and the answer is JUST FALSE (a failed "if") | read like "unless" (QA: a lifted bar says nothing, NOTHING) or as a scope limit (NOTHING)
-- src:5828 | 5. —(1) This Rule applies in relation to an action to enforce bearer debentures or to enforce debenture stock in respect of which the company has issued debenture stock bearer certificates. (2) Even though judgment has been given in the action and a certificate has been made in the action certifying the holders of such debentures or certificates referred to in paragraph (1), the title of any person claiming to be such a holder is (in the absence of notice of any defect in the title) sufficiently proved by the production of the debentures or debenture stock certificates (as the case may be) together with a certificate of identification signed by the person producing the debenture or certificate — ( a )
-- src:5829 | identifying the debenture or certificate produced; and
-- src:5830 | ( b )
-- src:5831 | certifying the person giving the person’s name and address who is the holder of the debenture or certificate.
@ref O 41 r 5(2) (src:5828-5831)
GIVEN `the debentures or debenture stock certificates are produced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a certificate of identification signed by the person producing them is produced with them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate of identification identifies the debenture or certificate produced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate of identification certifies the name and address of the holder of the debenture or certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is notice of a defect in the title` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 41 r 5(2) the title of the person claiming to be the holder is sufficiently proved` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `there is notice of a defect in the title`
           THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(in the absence of notice of any defect in the title)"
           IF     `the debentures or debenture stock certificates are produced`
              AND `a certificate of identification signed by the person producing them is produced with them`
              AND `the certificate of identification identifies the debenture or certificate produced`
              AND `the certificate of identification certifies the name and address of the holder of the debenture or certificate`
           THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the title is "sufficiently proved by" production with the certificate; the Rule does not say that title can be proved only that way

-- Rule 5(3): "Where such a debenture or certificate ... is produced in the chambers of the Judge, the solicitor
-- of the claimant in the action must cause to be endorsed on the debenture or certificate a notice stating"
-- three things.  The duty arises where it is produced in the Judge's chambers.
-- src:5832 | (3) Where such a debenture or certificate referred to in paragraph (1) is produced in the chambers of the Judge, the solicitor of the claimant in the action must cause to be endorsed on the debenture or certificate a notice stating — ( a )
@ref O 41 r 5(3) (src:5832)
GIVEN `the debenture or certificate is produced in the chambers of the Judge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 41 r 5(3) the claimant's solicitor's duty to cause a notice to be endorsed arises` MEANS
    IF `the debenture or certificate is produced in the chambers of the Judge`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where such a debenture or certificate referred to in paragraph (1) is produced in the chambers of the Judge"

DECLARE `o 41 r 5(3) the notice endorsed` HAS
    `o 41 r 5(3)(a) it states that the person named as the holder in the certificate of identification has been recorded in the chambers of the Judge as the holder` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 41 r 5(3)(b) it states that that person will, on producing the debenture or certificate, be entitled to receive payment of any dividend unless before payment a new holder proves the new holder's title in accordance with paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 41 r 5(3)(c) it states that if a new holder neglects to prove title the new holder may incur additional delay, trouble and expense in obtaining payment` IS A BOOLEAN

-- FORK QB | bare "must": the notice endorsed lacks a required statement | NOTHING | JUST FALSE for the compliance question
-- FORK QD | the duty does not arise (not produced in the Judge's chambers): NOTHING, with the companion above answering JUST FALSE | JUST TRUE
-- src:5832 | (3) Where such a debenture or certificate referred to in paragraph (1) is produced in the chambers of the Judge, the solicitor of the claimant in the action must cause to be endorsed on the debenture or certificate a notice stating — ( a )
-- src:5833 | that the person whose name and address is specified in the notice (being the person named as the holder of the debenture or certificate in the certificate of identification produced under paragraph (2)) has been recorded in the chambers of the Judge as the holder of the debenture or debenture stock certificate, as the case may be;
-- src:5834 | ( b )
-- src:5835 | that that person will, on producing the debenture or debenture stock certificate (as the case may be) be entitled to receive payment of any dividend in respect of that debenture or stock unless before payment a new holder proves the new holder’s title in accordance with paragraph (2); and
-- src:5836 | ( c )
-- src:5837 | that if a new holder neglects to prove the new holder’s title as mentioned in sub ‑ paragraph ( b ), the new holder may incur additional delay, trouble and expense in obtaining payment.
@ref O 41 r 5(3) (src:5832-5837)
GIVEN `the debenture or certificate is produced in the chambers of the Judge` IS A BOOLEAN
      notice IS A `o 41 r 5(3) the notice endorsed`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 41 r 5(3) the notice endorsed is as the Rule requires` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `the debenture or certificate is produced in the chambers of the Judge`)
           THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where such a debenture or certificate ... is produced in the chambers of the Judge" (the companion function says the duty does not arise)
           IF     notice's `o 41 r 5(3)(a) it states that the person named as the holder in the certificate of identification has been recorded in the chambers of the Judge as the holder`
              AND notice's `o 41 r 5(3)(b) it states that that person will, on producing the debenture or certificate, be entitled to receive payment of any dividend unless before payment a new holder proves the new holder's title in accordance with paragraph (2)`
              AND notice's `o 41 r 5(3)(c) it states that if a new holder neglects to prove title the new holder may incur additional delay, trouble and expense in obtaining payment`
           THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must" (QB); Rule 5(3) does not say what follows an incomplete notice

-- Rule 5(4): the claimant's solicitor "must preserve any certificate of identification ..., and must keep a
-- record of the debentures and debenture stock certificates so produced and of the names and addresses of the
-- persons producing them and of the holders ..., and, if the Court requires it, must verify the record by affidavit."
