-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 41 Rule 6 -- requirements in connection with payments`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Rule 6(1): "Where in an action to enforce any debentures or debenture stock an order is made for payment in
-- respect of the debentures or stock, the Accountant-General must not make a payment ... unless either there is
-- produced to him or her the certificate for which paragraph (2) provides or the Court has in the case in
-- question for special reason dispensed with the need for the certificate and directed payment to be made
-- without it."  First the "where": does the bar apply at all?
-- src:5840 | 6. —(1) Where in an action to enforce any debentures or debenture stock an order is made for payment in respect of the debentures or stock, the Accountant ‑ General must not make a payment in respect of any such debenture or stock unless either there is produced to him or her the certificate for which paragraph (2) provides or the Court has in the case in question for special reason dispensed with the need for the certificate and directed payment to be made without it. (2) For the purpose of obtaining such payment, the debenture or debenture stock certificate must be produced to the solicitor of the claimant in the action or to such other person as the Court may direct, and that solicitor or person must — ( a )
@ref O 41 r 6(1) (src:5840)
GIVEN `an order is made for payment in respect of the debentures or stock in an action to enforce them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 41 r 6(1) the bar on payment by the Accountant-General applies` MEANS
    IF `an order is made for payment in respect of the debentures or stock in an action to enforce them`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where in an action to enforce any debentures or debenture stock an order is made for payment in respect of the debentures or stock"

-- FORK QA | the certificate is produced or the Court has dispensed with it: the lifted bar grants nothing | JUST TRUE (the exception permits it)
-- src:5840 | 6. —(1) Where in an action to enforce any debentures or debenture stock an order is made for payment in respect of the debentures or stock, the Accountant ‑ General must not make a payment in respect of any such debenture or stock unless either there is produced to him or her the certificate for which paragraph (2) provides or the Court has in the case in question for special reason dispensed with the need for the certificate and directed payment to be made without it. (2) For the purpose of obtaining such payment, the debenture or debenture stock certificate must be produced to the solicitor of the claimant in the action or to such other person as the Court may direct, and that solicitor or person must — ( a )
@ref O 41 r 6(1) (src:5840)
GIVEN `an order is made for payment in respect of the debentures or stock in an action to enforce them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate for which paragraph (2) provides is produced to the Accountant-General` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has for special reason dispensed with the need for the certificate and directed payment without it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 41 r 6(1) the Accountant-General may make a payment in respect of the debenture or stock` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `an order is made for payment in respect of the debentures or stock in an action to enforce them`)
           THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (1) speaks only where an order for payment is made
           IF `the certificate for which paragraph (2) provides is produced to the Accountant-General` OR `the Court has for special reason dispensed with the need for the certificate and directed payment without it`
           THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless either there is produced to him or her the certificate ... or the Court has ... dispensed with the need for the certificate" lifts the bar and grants nothing (QA)
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Accountant-General must not make a payment in respect of any such debenture or stock"

-- The same paragraph as the question a party asks, "is the Accountant-General barred yet?": JUST TRUE while the bar bites, JUST FALSE once the certificate is produced or the Court has dispensed with it.
-- src:5840 | 6. —(1) Where in an action to enforce any debentures or debenture stock an order is made for payment in respect of the debentures or stock, the Accountant ‑ General must not make a payment in respect of any such debenture or stock unless either there is produced to him or her the certificate for which paragraph (2) provides or the Court has in the case in question for special reason dispensed with the need for the certificate and directed payment to be made without it. (2) For the purpose of obtaining such payment, the debenture or debenture stock certificate must be produced to the solicitor of the claimant in the action or to such other person as the Court may direct, and that solicitor or person must — ( a )
@ref O 41 r 6(1) (src:5840)
GIVEN `an order is made for payment in respect of the debentures or stock in an action to enforce them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate for which paragraph (2) provides is produced to the Accountant-General` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has for special reason dispensed with the need for the certificate and directed payment without it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 41 r 6(1) the Accountant-General is barred from making the payment` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `an order is made for payment in respect of the debentures or stock in an action to enforce them`)
           THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where in an action to enforce any debentures or debenture stock an order is made for payment in respect of the debentures or stock" (the condition is not met)
           IF `the certificate for which paragraph (2) provides is produced to the Accountant-General` OR `the Court has for special reason dispensed with the need for the certificate and directed payment without it`
           THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless either there is produced to him or her the certificate ... or the Court has ... dispensed with the need for the certificate" -- the bar ends
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- Rule 6(2): "For the purpose of obtaining such payment, the debenture or debenture stock certificate must be
-- produced to the solicitor of the claimant in the action or to such other person as the Court may direct,
-- and that solicitor or person must (a) endorse ... a memorandum of payment; and (b) make and sign a
-- certificate certifying that the statement set out in the certificate has been endorsed ..., and send the
-- certificate to the Accountant-General."
DECLARE `o 41 r 6(2) what has been done` HAS
    `o 41 r 6(2) the debenture or certificate is produced to the solicitor of the claimant or to the person the Court directs` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 41 r 6(2)(a) a memorandum of payment is endorsed on it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 41 r 6(2)(b) a certificate certifying the endorsement is made and signed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 41 r 6(2)(b) the certificate is sent to the Accountant-General` IS A BOOLEAN

